1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:08,684
Every reaction in this table is the same reaction: nucleophilic substitution on bromoethane, with eight different nucleophiles.

2
00:00:08,684 --> 00:00:12,500
Aqueous potassium hydroxide gives ethanol.

3
00:00:12,500 --> 00:00:15,260
Potassium cyanide gives a nitrile.

4
00:00:15,260 --> 00:00:18,320
Silver cyanide gives an isocyanide.

5
00:00:18,320 --> 00:00:20,559
Excess ammonia gives an amine.

6
00:00:20,559 --> 00:00:25,377
Sodium ethoxide gives an ether, the Williamson synthesis.

7
00:00:25,377 --> 00:00:27,890
A thiolate gives a thioether.

8
00:00:27,890 --> 00:00:34,114
Potassium nitrite gives an alkyl nitrite, and silver nitrite a nitroalkane.

